One might see this as conditional fulfillment of the earlier word. Tyre was opposing Babylon, and then stopped doing so, and so God's immediate purposes in sending an army against it were removed. And yet, for what Tyre did to Israel, how it treated those it traded with, and what it thought, it would eventually be wiped out as a nation.\
