The stubbornness Isaiah identifies \'97 making plans but not YHWH's, alliances but not of YHWH's Spirit \'97 gets its theological diagnosis here. Why is such planning stubborn? Because it treats human powers as if their agency were ultimate, as if their plans could succeed apart from YHWH's word. The crocodile's claim is the implicit theology behind every such alliance.\
