\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The context of this conversation, centering as it does on Ezekiel 29, makes thinking about reading Ezekiel 29 more salient in a natural way.\
And in many ways, the second oracle is about how to read Ezekiel.\
But the first oracle very much is not.\
While applying Ezekiel to the world of today requires great caution, there are definitely points of contact.\'a0 A long dominant superpower.\'a0 The possibility of new actors to think the balance of power now favors them and they can do as they wish with none to hinder - and that, alongside a temptation to believe they built their own power, whether those actors are AI companies or AIs themselves given the tendency to use AI in its own development these days.\
